    <p class="stack-note">Built for MSPs on ConnectWise and Hudu. The ConnectWise and Hudu connections are built to their published APIs; their first checks against live accounts are part of the pilot. Product names belong to their owners, and no endorsement is implied.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="setup wrap" aria-labelledby="h-setup">
    <div class="setup-copy">
      <h2 id="h-setup">Three steps per technician.</h2>
      <p class="sub">One installer per technician PC. Your ScreenTrail owner connects ConnectWise and Hudu once in the web admin, and the app's setup guide walks each technician through the rest.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="stepbox"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>Install on each technician's PC</h3><p>One installer for the app and its capture service.</p></div></li>
      <li class="stepbox"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>Activate with an invite code</h3><p>Your ScreenTrail owner invites each technician; the code works once, on one PC.</p>
        <div class="code"><span class="fn">Setup · Activate</span>Invite code <em>XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX</em></div></div></li>
      <li class="stepbox"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>Pick the remote tools</h3><p>Choose which tools start a session. The ConnectWise and Hudu connection is already there.</p>
        <div class="code"><span class="fn">Setup · Remote tools</span><span class="cbo"><span class="cb on"></span>ScreenConnect</span><span class="cbo"><span class="cb on"></span>Remote Desktop</span><span class="cbo"><span class="cb"></span>AnyDesk</span></div></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <MaskBand label="masked on the PC" />

  <section class="privacy wrap" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="h-privacy">
    <h2 id="h-privacy">Built for the security review your clients will ask for.</h2>
    <div class="privacy-grid">
      <div>
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/></svg><h3>No always-on capture</h3><p>Only while a remote tool is in front, with the pill on screen the whole time.</p></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="9" width="16" height="6" rx="1"/><path d="M4 5h16M4 19h10"/></svg><h3>Secrets masked on the PC</h3><p>Passwords, card numbers and keys it reads are painted out before storage.</p></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="11" rx="3"/><path d="M5 11a7 7 0 0014 0M12 18v3"/></svg><h3>Voice stays local</h3><p>Transcribed on the PC. The end user's voice is not recorded.</p></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v6c0 4-3 7.5-7 9-4-1.5-7-5-7-9V6z"/></svg><h3>A local-only switch</h3><p>Nothing is sent for drafting; your ScreenTrail owner can lock it on.</p></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 018 0v3"/></svg><h3>Encrypted at rest</h3><p>Sessions in an encrypted store; PSA credentials in an encrypted vault.</p></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 8v4l3 2"/></svg><h3>Kept as long as you say</h3><p>Retention set by the MSP; discarding a session deletes its captures.</p></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="privacy-more">
          <a class="btn btn-line" href="/security/">How ScreenTrail handles data</a>
          <a class="btn btn-line" href={`${site.repo}/tree/main/docs/security`}>Read the privacy pack on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="plain-fig">
        <div class="frame-fig"><Image src={panel} width={404} height={585} widths={[404, 808]} sizes="404px" loading="lazy" alt="What's being captured right now: capturing ScreenConnect, local-only on, nothing suppressed, the redaction queue, frames dropped, egress blocked, the policy in force, and a Copy diagnostics button." /></div>
        <figcaption>Any technician can open "What's being captured right now?" from the tray.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pilot wrap" id="pilot" data-pill="published" aria-labelledby="h-pilot">
    <h2 id="h-pilot">The note this page wrote.</h2>
    <p class="sub mt">You have just followed a session. Here is its draft. The follow-up is yours.</p>
    <article class="final-note" aria-labelledby="h-become">
      <div class="fn-main note">
        <div class="fn-head"><h3 id="h-become">Become a pilot MSP</h3><span class="chip">To: you · internal note</span></div>
        <div class="fn-sec"><h4>Problem</h4><p>Technicians write notes from memory after the session. Steps go missing, time goes unbilled, and the fix is never written up for the next person.</p></div>
        <div class="fn-sec"><h4>Steps</h4>
          <ol>
            <li>Followed the session: the screen, the clicks and the technician's voice.</li>
            <li>Masked passwords, keys and card numbers on the PC.</li>
            <li>Drafted the note, the time entry and a KB article.</li>
            <li>Waited for a person to check it and publish.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="fn-sec"><h4>Targets for the pilot</h4>
          <span class="flagnote">Not measured yet: these are the pilot's targets, not results.</span>
          <dl class="targets">
            <div><dt>60%</dt><dd>less time writing notes, at least</dd></div>
            <div><dt>&lt;25%</dt><dd>of a draft's words changed before publishing, at most</dd></div>
            <div><dt>80%</dt><dd>of remote sessions captured without starting one by hand</dd></div>
            <div><dt>0</dt><dd>passwords or personal data in a published note</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="fn-sec"><h4>Follow-ups</h4>
          <p>A small number of MSPs, real tickets, and a plain account of where it falls short.</p>
          <dl class="fit">
            <div><dt>Team</dt><dd>3 to 30 technicians working tickets over remote sessions</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>ConnectWise PSA, with Hudu if you use it; ScreenConnect or Remote Desktop</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Before</dt><dd>A short measure of how long notes take today</dd></div>
            <div><dt>During</dt><dd>A few weeks of real use, with a direct line to the people building it</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="fn-side" aria-labelledby="h-form">
        <h3 class="form-h" id="h-form">Tell us about your team</h3>
        <form class="pilot-form" method="post" action="/api/pilot" id="pilot-form">
          <label>Your name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required maxlength={limits.name} /></label>
          <label>Work email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required pattern="[^\s@]+@[A-Za-z0-9\-]+(\.[A-Za-z0-9\-]+)+" title="An email address like name@company.com" maxlength={limits.email} /></label>
          <label>Company<input name="company" autocomplete="organization" required maxlength={limits.company} /></label>
          <fieldset class="choice">
            <legend>Technicians</legend>
            <div class="opts">{choices.technicians.map((c) => <label><input type="radio" name="technicians" value={c} required /><span>{c}</span></label>)}</div>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset class="choice">
            <legend>PSA</legend>
            <div class="opts">{choices.psa.map((c) => <label><input type="radio" name="psa" value={c} required /><span>{c}</span></label>)}</div>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset class="choice">
            <legend>Main remote tool</legend>
            <div class="opts">{choices.tool.map((c) => <label><input type="radio" name="tool" value={c} required /><span>{c}</span></label>)}</div>
          </fieldset>
          <label><span>Anything else <span class="opt">(optional)</span></span><textarea name="message" maxlength={limits.message} rows="3"></textarea></label>
          <div class="hp" hidden><label>Leave this empty<input name="hp_trap" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label></div>
          <p class="form-reply">We usually reply within two working days.</p>
          <button class="publish-btn" type="submit">Send to ScreenTrail <kbd aria-hidden="true">Ctrl+Enter</kbd></button>
          <p class="form-fine">We use this only to reply about the pilot, and the site keeps no copy. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></p>
        </form>
      </aside>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>

